    "DECISION_NOTE": "Chosen after test_edit_levels_v5.py, run 4aa278d54d (committed as v5/stimulus_levels_data/4aa278d54d/), and a visual check of its viewer. Method A4_haze_cc_rgb: contrast down with v4's brightness-equated haze (haze_eq), contrast up with the same blend run backwards on RGB (v4's m_contrast_up, 'dehaze_rgb'), and at every contrast level a chroma factor that restores the scene's mean saturation, so the contrast levels leave saturation unchanged. Colour: v4's CIELAB chroma edit in both directions. Levels: definition (b), equal steps in corpus SD solved per scene, at +-1/3, +-2/3 and +-1 SD on both features, so the unedited original sits in the middle of both ladders and 'edited' points both ways. No clipping budget: the upward contrast levels clip (reported, not used to cap or exclude), and the +3 images were judged acceptable. All 47 v4 scenes, none set aside, for variety. No grid block in v5.",
